1
00:00:00,729 --> 00:00:02,059
(Amy:)Bye.

2
00:00:02,063 --> 00:00:03,863
Oh! Good news, gentlemen.

3
00:00:03,865 --> 00:00:05,735
(Sheldon:)Amy's at a conference
this weekend,

4
00:00:05,734 --> 00:00:09,204
(Sheldon:)which means I'm available
to be entertained, hmm.

5
00:00:09,204 --> 00:00:13,844
As today's youth might put it:
Who wants to get their Sheld-on?

6
00:00:13,842 --> 00:00:16,942
(Howard:)Bernie and I are getting
the house ready for the remodel.

7
00:00:16,945 --> 00:00:19,045
(Howard:)We could always use
an extra pair of hands.

8
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:21,347
(Sheldon:)That sounds awful. Raj?

9
00:00:21,349 --> 00:00:24,119
(Raj:)Uh, I've got time booked in
the telescope room all weekend

10
00:00:24,119 --> 00:00:25,219
(Raj:)scanning for rogue planets.

11
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,920
(Raj:)You're more than welcome
to join me.

12
00:00:26,922 --> 00:00:28,892
(Sheldon:)That's the one to beat.
Leonard?

13
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:32,490
(Leonard:)Oh, if anything,
I'm trying to get my Sheld-off.

14
00:00:32,494 --> 00:00:34,964
(Sheldon:)Well, then it looks like we have
a winner. Congratulations.

15
00:00:34,963 --> 00:00:37,693
(Raj:)Well, I should warn you,
it's just looking at data

16
00:00:37,699 --> 00:00:39,929
(Raj:)for hours and hours
on a computer screen.

17
00:00:39,935 --> 00:00:42,205
(Sheldon:)Uh, stop selling it, kid.
You won.

18
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:46,945
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

